    "explanation": "Both sides' evidence converges on the same arithmetic, and the outcome for the rider is a full refund of the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line.\n\nDRIVER — your arrival was genuine, but the fee still cannot stand. The trip record carries your driver_arrived event at 2026-08-17T12:48:56 (EV-TRIP-03104), and your own GPS trace (EV-GPS-03104) puts you inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from that same second, holding 11 consecutive qualifying fixes at the 10 s cadence. So POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied, and I reject any suggestion of a false 'I'm Here' tap: the marker timestamp coincides exactly with the first qualifying in-geofence fix (dwell_start_offset_sec = 0.0), so POL-NS-05's distance and speed triggers are not engaged and no false-arrival referral is recorded against you.\n\nThe charge fails on the waiting period. Under POL-NS-01(c) the free waiting period in force for this trip is trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 seconds, and the dwell clock runs from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the arrival tap. Your trace shows one continuous in-geofence run of 95 seconds, from 12:48:56 to 12:50:31, against the 180 seconds required — a shortfall of 85 seconds — and you terminated at 12:50:34, before the period elapsed. POL-NS-06 makes that shortfall a strict-liability refund of the cancellation-fee line whether or not the rider was present or responsive, and it expressly allows no driver compensation on this route; POL-NS-07 pays a driver only where POL-NS-01 holds in full, which it does not. The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) cannot help either: the trace contains a single in-geofence interval (run_count = 1), so there is no second interval to sum, and the traffic_advisory it also requires, EV-ADVIS-03104-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — an absence that can be cited but carries no fact.\n\nRIDER — you are refunded the full SGD 4.50. That is the cancellation_fee line on EV-FARE-03104 and the total_charged figure (SGD 4.50, with base fare, platform fee, distance, time and waiting-time fee all at SGD 0.00), and it equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. Your 24 qualifying fixes (12:47:45–12:51:12) place your device between 3.2 m and 9.4 m of the pickup pin, well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and they corroborate your 12:49:56 message 'im at the lobby, coming out'. I note the driver's counterparty statement that you were 'not visible' is contradicted by that track; the statement carries no weight_multiplier and enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence cap. Your exoneration under POL-NS-04 does not independently fire — the driver replied 'ok' 15 seconds after your message, inside the 120 s window — but that makes no difference, because POL-NS-06 refunds on the shortfall alone.\n\nOn integrity and escalation: no POL-NS-08 limb fires. There is no clock skew (the marker and the first in-geofence fix share the timestamp 12:48:56), no trace gap (max_gap_sec = 0.0, 59 fixes, 100% coverage, rider track present), no chat defect (2 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count = 2, sequence intact), and no fare defect. The deciding facts — the 95 s dwell against the 180 s minimum — rest on EV-GPS-03104 and EV-TRIP-03104, both at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0, and no POL-NS-09 trigger (confidence, direct contradiction on arrival/dwell/presence, repeat-party disputes, anti-farming, sole impaired evidence) applies. No escalation, and no referral: POL-NS-05(ii), POL-RD-06(c) and POL-RD-09(4) each require facts this record does not carry, and the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW is one POL-NS-01(d) recognises, so no mis-coded-reason item arises.\n\nThe monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this refund executes automatically; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
